-- title:
--   Vanishing in Q ⊗_S Q versus membership in (I(x), I(y))
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a commutative ring and $C$ a commutative $S$-algebra, and let $\theta : S[\![x_1,x_2]\!] \to C$ be a surjective homomorphism of $S$-algebras, where $S[\![x_1,x_2]\!]$ denotes the multivariate power series ring on the index set $\mathrm{Fin}\,2$. Assume that each $\theta(X_i)$ is nilpotent in $C$ and that $\theta$ is given by evaluation at this family: for every $G$, $\theta G = \mathrm{adicEval}\,\bot\,(i \mapsto \theta(X_i))\,G$, where $\mathrm{adicEval}\,J\,x$ is the two-step evaluation `MvPowerSeries.eval₂` of the structure map $S \to C$ together with the family $x$, taken with the discrete uniformity on $S$ and the ideal $J$ on $C$, here $J = \bot$. Let $I$ be an ideal of $S[\![x_1,x_2]\!]$ containing $\ker \theta$, and let $G$ be a power series in two blocks of two variables, indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,2 \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,2$. Write $\pi : C \to C/\theta(I)$ for the quotient map of $S$-modules attached to the image ideal $\theta(I)$, restricted to scalars in $S$. Then the image of $\mathrm{adicEval}\,\bot$ of $G$ at the family sending the $j$-th variable of the first block to $\theta(X_j) \otimes 1$ and the $j$-th variable of the second block to $1 \otimes \theta(X_j)$, an element of $C \otimes_S C$, under $\pi \otimes \pi$ is zero if and only if $G$ lies in the ideal of $S[\![x_1,x_2,y_1,y_2]\!]$ generated by the union of the image of $I$ under the substitution $X_l \mapsto X_{\mathrm{inl}\,l}$ and the image of $I$ under $X_l \mapsto X_{\mathrm{inr}\,l}$.
--
--   This is the commutative-algebra step identifying the kernel of the map $S[\![x,y]\!] \to Q \otimes_S Q$, $Q = C/\theta(I)$, with the ideal generated by $I$ in the $x$-variables together with $I$ in the $y$-variables; it rests on the fact that nilpotence of the $\theta(X_i)$ makes everything factor through finite free truncations, for which the kernel of a tensor product of two surjections is the sum of the two partial kernels. It is used in the construction of the scheme representing a subgroup ideal of a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module, where the group law on the quotient has to be recognised as coming from the comultiplication modulo the ideal in each block of variables.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvFormalGroup_map_mkQ_adicEval_sumElim_tmul_eq_zero_iff_mem_span_image_subst.lean

